    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="Inscr.">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IEm">I Em</ref> Inscr.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="I Em. Inscr." corresp="#wit-h">Eadmundes cyninges asetnysse.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="I Em. Inscr." corresp="#wit-d">Her onginneð Eadmundes gerædnes.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="I Em. Inscr." corresp="#wit-g-b-part-prol">Eadmundes gerædnes.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">Her onginneð Eadmundes gerædnes.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">Here begins Edmund's ordinance.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">(Hier beginnt D) König Eadmunds Verordnung (Satzung H).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Here begins, D) King Edmund's ordinance (statute, H).</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Base text K = H (Textus Roffensis f. 44, c. 1125, after II Ew). Also in D (CCCC 201 p. 96), B (CCCC 383 f. 78), G (Cotton Nero A I f. 88v, breaks off in the Prologue), Ld and Quadr. Heading in red in H, D and G.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
